      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GINNIVAN (1) is on the back-up after narrowly going down in the Nicopolis Stakes last week. That followed another narrow second placing to the same horse - Haida Gwaii - and he will appreciate her absence here. Lots of weight but gets in well after the claim. POND MASTER (5) resumed over 1000m at this track last start and was too good for his rivals, scoring by a nose. Has never missed the frame second-up and looks sure to be in the finish again. HEY PINO (7) gave the leaders a start last start and made little impact in the straight when sixth, beaten 8 lengths, over this journey at this track. Finds a nice race and can figure in the finish. PLATINUM SHOT (3) will be better with the first-up run out of the way, draws well and warrants major respect due to a second-up record that reads 5 starts for a win, a second and two thirds. COUNTRY GOD (8) was out of the money when resuming from a spell last start over 1200m at this track, beaten 2.5 lengths, but can improve from the low draw.",
